{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"Case-splitting on `hr` before constructing the two simulation directions avoids eliminating the same relation twice. Anonymous constructor notation further reduces syntax without changing elaboration behavior or proof structure.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro h\\n  use @ChoiceBisim _ _ defs, .choice h\\n  intro _ _ hr _\\n  cases hr with\\n  | choice h =>\\n    constructor <;> intro s' ht\\n    · cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨q', ht, h'⟩ := h.follow_fst ht\\n        exact ⟨q', .choiceL ht, .bisim h'⟩\\n      | choiceR ht => exact ⟨s', .choiceR ht, .bisim (.refl _)⟩\\n    · cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨p', ht, h'⟩ := h.follow_snd ht\\n        exact ⟨p', .choiceL ht, .bisim h'⟩\\n      | choiceR ht => exact ⟨s', .choiceR ht, .bisim (.refl _)⟩\\n  | bisim h =>\\n    constructor <;> intro s' ht\\n    · obtain ⟨q', ht, h'⟩ := h.follow_fst ht\\n      exact ⟨q', ht, .bisim h'⟩\\n    · obtain ⟨p', ht, h'⟩ := h.follow_snd ht\\n      exact ⟨p', ht, .bisim h'⟩\"}"}}
